{
  "id": "150d2fdc-b239-491a-8189-98bc3701caf8",
  "productId": "openmrs",
  "title": "Bill Line Item Pricing Logic",
  "updatedAt": 1793522610813,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "dr1BMheaEVH3SVqI",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "Where in the code are bill line items priced from a stock item or billable service, and how does that pricing get applied?",
      "generation": "g-ab363e",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Pricing of a bill line item happens in two places: automatically from orders (server-side strategies), and manually via REST/frontend.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## 1. Stock item path — drug orders",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "`DrugOrderBillingStrategy` handles `DrugOrder`s and resolves the price from the stock item linked to the ordered drug [1]:",
          "citations": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "- It looks up stock items via `stockManagementService.getStockItemByDrug(drugId)`; no stock item means no line item at all [2]\n- `resolvePrice(stockItem)` asks `itemPriceService.getItemPrice(stockItem)`, takes the first result's price, otherwise falls back to the stock item's `purchasePrice`, otherwise `BigDecimal.ZERO` [3]\n- Quantity comes from `drugOrder.getQuantity()`; the line item is marked `EXEMPTED` or `PENDING` by the exemption check, then `lineItem.setItem(stockItem)` ties the line to the stock item [4]",
          "citations": [
            2,
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## 2. Billable service path — test orders",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "`TestOrderBillingStrategy` handles `TestOrder`s by finding an enabled `BillableService` whose concept UUID matches the order's concept, then pricing it [5]:",
          "citations": [
            5
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "- Search is built from a `BillableServiceSearch` with `setConceptUuid` and `setServiceStatus(ENABLED)`; the first match wins [6]\n- `resolvePrice(billableService)` uses `itemPriceService.getServicePrice(billableService)` and returns the first price, or `BigDecimal.ZERO` if there are none [7]\n- Quantity is hard-coded to `1`, and the service is attached with `lineItem.setBillableService(billableService)` [8]",
          "citations": [
            6,
            7,
            8
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## 3. Where the price actually lands on the line item",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Both strategies funnel into `createLineItem(price, quantity, status, order)` in the shared base class, which is the point where the resolved `BigDecimal` is written onto `BillLineItem.setPrice` along with quantity, status, `lineItemOrder = 0` and the originating order [9]. The subclass then adds the item/service.",
          "citations": [
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The line item is put into a new `Bill` and persisted by `createBill(...)`, which sets patient, `PENDING` status, cashier, cash point and visit, calls `bill.addLineItem(lineItem)` and `billService.saveBill(bill)` [10]. `Bill.addLineItem(StockItem, price, priceName, quantity)` is the manual equivalent and also requires a non-null price [11].",
          "citations": [
            10,
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## 4. Where the candidate prices come from",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "`ItemPriceService` exposes the two lookups used above [12]:",
          "citations": [
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "- `getItemPrice(stockItem)` queries `CashierItemPrice` by `item` equality, ordered by `id` descending — so \"first\" means the most recently created price api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/impl/ItemPriceServiceImpl.java\n- `getServicePrice(billableService)` does the same on `billableService` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/impl/ItemPriceServiceImpl.java",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A `CashierItemPrice` can point at either a `StockItem` (`item`) or a `BillableService` (`billableService`), plus an optional `paymentMode`, and holds the `price` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/model/CashierItemPrice.java. `BillableService` owns its prices as a `servicePrices` list api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/model/BillableService.java. Persistence: prices are stored in `cashier_item_price` with `item_id`, `service_id`, `payment_mode` and a not-null `price` api/src/main/resources/Bill.hbm.xml; the line item row `cashier_bill_line_item` stores the resolved `price`, `price_name`, an optional link back to the chosen `CashierItemPrice` (`price_id`) and the `item`/`service_id` api/src/main/resources/Bill.hbm.xml.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## 6. Manual / API path",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "When the UI or another client creates a line item directly, the price is whatever is sent: `BillLineItemResource.setPriceValue` accepts a `Double`/`Integer` and converts it to `BigDecimal`, rejecting other types omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/BillLineItemResource.java. The `item` and `billableService` setters just resolve UUIDs to entities — no server-side repricing omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/BillLineItemResource.java. Note the `priceUuid` setter in that resource is effectively a stub: `itemPrice` is declared as `null` and the branch can never run, so it never links a `CashierItemPrice` omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/BillLineItemResource.java.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Client side, the app treats `price` as a plain stored number: bill totals multiply `item.price * item.quantity` over unvoided line items src/helpers/functions.ts, and the `LineItem` type carries `price`, `priceName` and `priceUuid` src/types/index.ts. Service prices reach the UI as `servicePrices:(uuid,name,price,paymentMode)` on the `billableService` endpoint src/billing.resource.ts. There is a configured `priceUuid` in the config schema, but the comment there says it is currently unused in code src/config-schema.ts.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## 7. How it flows",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "```mermaid\n---\ntitle: Line item pricing\n---\nflowchart TD\n  order[\"Order saved\"] --> strategy{\"Order type\"}\n  strategy -->|DrugOrder| drug[\"DrugOrderBillingStrategy\"]\n  strategy -->|TestOrder| test[\"TestOrderBillingStrategy\"]\n  drug --> findStock[\"getStockItemByDrug\"]\n  findStock --> itemPrice[\"getItemPrice(stockItem)\"]\n  itemPrice --> fallback{\"Price found\"}\n  fallback -->|no| purchase[\"stockItem.purchasePrice\"]\n  fallback -->|yes| priceVal[\"first CashierItemPrice\"]\n  purchase --> priceVal2[\"BigDecimal\"]\n  test --> findService[\"getBillableServices by concept, ENABLED\"]\n  findService --> svcPrice[\"getServicePrice(billableService)\"]\n  svcPrice --> priceVal2\n  priceVal --> priceVal2\n  priceVal2 --> create[\"createLineItem sets price, quantity, status, order\"]\n  create --> bill[\"createBill adds item/service, saveBill\"]\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## 8. Ordering caveats worth knowing",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- Price selection ignores payment mode and retirement: both DAO-style queries order by `id` descending and the strategies blindly take `get(0)` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/billing/impl/DrugOrderBillingStrategy.java api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/billing/impl/TestOrderBillingStrategy.java.\n- Exempt orders still get a priced line item, just with status `EXEMPTED` rather than a zero price api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/billing/impl/AbstractDefaultOrderBillingStrategy.java.\n- Rounding adjustments follow the same pattern, setting `price` on a rounding line item api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/util/RoundingUtil.java.\n- `BillLineItem.getTotal()` is simply `price * quantity` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/model/BillLineItem.java.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
